<div class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="article">
<p>This notice explains what the Jos Mental Health Conference (JMHC) collects through this website and how it is used.</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>Only what you type into our forms: for example your name, email, phone number, organisation and message. We do not ask for health information, and please do not send any through the website.</p>
<h2>How we use it</h2>
<p>To reply to you, to register your interest, to process pledges and partnership enquiries, and, if you subscribe, to send conference updates. We do not sell or share your details with sponsors or anyone else.</p>
<h2>Where it is kept</h2>
<p>Form messages are delivered by email to the JMHC secretariat through a form service (Web3Forms). Visitor statistics come from Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies or track you across sites.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can unsubscribe at any time, or ask us to correct or delete your details, by emailing {{ site.email }}. We follow the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023.</p>
</div></div></div>
